fieldExtension -- a fix to the failure of map(GaloisField,GaloisField) function when Variable option is used
************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fieldExtension(L, K)
  * Inputs:
      * K, a *note Galois field: (Macaulay2Doc)GaloisField,, a finite field
      * L, a *note Galois field: (Macaulay2Doc)GaloisField,, a field extension
        of $K$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the natural ring map $K \to
        L$.

Description
===========

The usual *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map, function is not working properly when
the generators of a *note GaloisField: (Macaulay2Doc)GaloisField, are
designated. For example,



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K1 = GF(8); L1 = GF(64);                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : K2 = GF(8, Variable=>b); L2 = GF(64, Variable=>c);                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : map(L1, K1) --correct natural map                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                    5    4    2                                              |
|o5 = map (L1, K1, {a  + a  + a  + 1})                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : RingMap L1 <-- K1                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : try map(L2, K2) then << "correct map" else << "error: not implemented:  |
|correct map                                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|maps between non-Conway Galois fields";                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This function is a fix for that. See following example



+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : K2 = GF(8, Variable=>b); L2 = GF(64, Variable=>c);|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : fieldExtension(L2, K2)                            |
|                                                       |
|                    5    4    2                        |
|o9 = map (L2, K2, {c  + c  + c  + 1})                  |
|                                                       |
|o9 : RingMap L2 <-- K2                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

The function is implemented by composing the isomorphism $K_2\cong K_1$, the
natural embedding $K_1\to L_1$ and the isomorphism $L_1\cong L_2$.





Caveat
======

The function depends on the implementation of map(GaloisField,GaloisField).



